// DISCRIMINATION CASE 1 (grep gets it WRONG -- it calls this "buggy").
//
// This is a *response*-sum spend-cap policy: the temporal sum quantifies over
// `Transfer::response` rows (settled completions only), so in-flight (issued,
// not-yet-responded) transfers are invisible to the sum.  A keyword/pattern
// scan ("response-sum => in-flight invisible => UNSAFE") flags this as buggy.
//
// ROTN's verdict depends on the *concurrency bound K* (the client-side
// request-pool size), which a keyword scan cannot see:
//
//   K = 1  ->  SAFE.    At most one transfer is in flight, so the parallel-
//                       fire race (N un-settled fires all passing the guard)
//                       is structurally impossible: a fire is admitted only
//                       while inflight < 1, i.e. when settled + amount <= cap,
//                       and that one in-flight fire settles to <= cap.
//   K >= 2 ->  UNSAFE.  Two or more un-settled fires can each pass the guard
//                       (settled still 0) and settle to > cap.  Witness at
//                       K=3: {completed: 0, inflight: 3}  (3 x 100 = 300 > 200).
//
// The SAME policy text is SAFE or UNSAFE purely by the bound the environment
// imposes on in-flight concurrency -- exactly the kind of context a grep
// cannot model.  See docs/discrimination.md.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace (alert_total_transfer_over_200 schema).
// TransferInput carries `amount: Long`; TransferOutput is empty.

@id("discrimination_response_sum_bounded")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum a for (a: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::response{ input.amount: a } && tp(t))
    )) <= 200
};
